        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(skills): background lifecycle curator for workshop-created skills",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nSkill Workshop's capture ladder is complete (`/learn`, default-on suggestions, autonomous capture), but there is no maintenance half: agent-created skills accumulate forever with no usage tracking, staleness handling, or cleanup path. Issue #95516 describes the resulting skill bloat.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds a background lifecycle curator for **workshop-created skills only** (skills whose applied proposal has `createdBy: \"skill-workshop\"`; manually authored skills are never touched):\n\n- **Usage tracking** — the existing `skill.used` trusted diagnostic event now persists aggregate per-skill usage (`skill_usage` table, shared state DB, Kysely). A trusted-listeners-only delivery path keeps accounting alive when optional diagnostics are disabled.\n- **Lifecycle states** — `active → stale` (30 days unused) `→ archived` (90 days unused), fixed constants, zero new config keys. Archived skills are filtered out of skill snapshots via one query per snapshot build; **files are never moved, edited, or deleted**. Pinned skills bypass all transitions. Archived → active only via explicit restore. Lifecycle identity is the canonical skill file, so same-named skills across agent workspaces never collide.\n- **Scheduling** — daily sweep owned by the gateway maintenance timers (same pattern as media cleanup: delayed initial run, in-flight guard, logged errors), with explicit persisted state in `skill_curator_state`. Disabled in manual-RPC gateway tests.\n- **Overlap detection** — deterministic token-similarity report (workspace-scoped, no LLM, no config); suggestions only, merging stays with the operator through the normal proposal approval flow.\n- **Surfaces** — `openclaw skills curator [status|pin|unpin|restore]` CLI with `--json` and gateway fallback; additive gateway methods `skills.curator.status` (operator.read) and `pin/unpin/restore` (operator.admin); warn-only doctor finding when the curator hasn't completed a sweep for 7 days.\n\nDeliberately narrower than #95516's full proposal: no auto-optimization, no auto-delete, no config surface (fixed 30d/90d vs the issue's configurable 180d/365d).\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers with long-lived agents get automatic hygiene for accumulated agent-created skills: stale ones are flagged, long-unused ones drop out of context (recoverable at any time), and overlap candidates are surfaced. Manually authored skills, pinned skills, and all skill files on disk are untouched. No new configuration.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- All touched suites green on Blacksmith Testbox: [full run](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28828318238) (curator lifecycle matrix — transitions, pinned bypass, archived-not-auto-reactivated, multi-workspace same-name skills, ghost-row pruning, workspace-scoped overlap; skills loading/snapshot filtering incl. state-DB-unavailable fail-open; gateway maintenance/close/runtime wiring; method scopes; doctor contribution; state-DB schema; CLI) and [privacy-fix rerun](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28828913884) (diagnostic-events trusted-only delivery, tool-hook e2e path-free public payload assertions, curator).\n- Structured review (Codex/gpt-5.5) ran to clean across three fix rounds; accepted findings fixed: multi-workspace skill-key collision wedging the sweep, mixed file/name usage scoping, absolute skill paths leaking to public diagnostic listeners, and skill loading hard-failing when the state DB is unavailable (caught on Testbox).\n- tsgo core + core.test lanes clean; oxfmt clean; `pnpm docs:map:gen` regenerated.\n- Docs: `docs/tools/skill-workshop.md` \"Lifecycle curation\" section.\n\nScoped implementation of the retirement half of #95516 (commented there; issue asks for a broader system — see comment for what is intentionally out of scope).\n",
        "branch": "claude/fervent-khayyam-106224",
